Text:
```
		this._register(this._textAreaInput.onKeyDown((e: IKeyboardEvent) => {
			this._viewController.emitKeyDown(e);
		}));
```

Search for `((e: ` (with a trailing space). Toggle whole words on, observe there are no matches.

When https://github.com/Microsoft/vscode/issues/25780 was closed, the history navigator stopped re-ordering when adding an existing element.

Previously with ArraySet, the set method had:

```typescript
set(element T): void {
    this.unset(element);
    this._elements.push(element);
}
```

since native Sets don't have this property, this needs to happen manually in the cases where we expect adding an item to the set to affect its order, like in history.ts.

This is caused by 3a3f0e41968ddd3cef6c1e4a090ca8ef8bc6b049 which will be reverted from master.

The problem is that 3a3f0e41968ddd3cef6c1e4a090ca8ef8bc6b049 makes it appear that we are in a good shape to support `"editor.selectionForeground"`, which we are not. Before 3a3f0e41968ddd3cef6c1e4a090ca8ef8bc6b049, we supported it for high contrast themes because that is an accessibility must. But we should not advertise this, as changing the selection foreground results in repainting all the lines when changing the selection.

